-- Step 25: supplier bills.
-- track: B
--
-- The CREATE TABLE / index statements are generated by drizzle-kit from
-- src/modules/*/schema.ts. The sections marked "hand-written" are not managed by Drizzle.
-- Reverse with the file of the same name in drizzle/down.
--
-- A supplier's bill says what the supplier asks to be paid: for goods already received (each
-- line is so much of one line of a posted goods received note, at the supplier's price), or for
-- a service or expense (a line charged to an account). It is a draft the app writes. Posting it
-- is one act of the database, app.post_supplier_bill:
--
--   debit   Goods received not invoiced     what the billed goods came into stock at
--   debit   or credit  Purchase price differences   the bill's price less that (the founder's
--                                           decision, 2026-11-15: the stock value is not touched)
--   debit   the expense accounts            services and expenses, with the province's tax on them
--   debit   Sales tax receivable            input tax, where the company and the supplier are registered
--   credit  the withholding payable accounts   tax withheld, where the company deducts it
--   credit  Trade payables                  what is left owed to the supplier
--
-- Every rate is read from the dated tax tables for the bill's date, by the database, when the
-- bill is posted: tax_rates for input tax, withholding_rules for what is withheld. The app works
-- the same figures out beforehand with src/modules/tax/rules.ts to show them; a bill whose
-- figures are not what the tables give is refused. Nothing withheld is kept anywhere but in
-- withholding_entries, which only this function writes.
--
-- Tax is withheld only by a company that has switched it on (purchase_settings.withholding_on;
-- the founder's decision, 2026-11-15: off until switched on).
--
-- The owner and an accountant write and post bills; the auditor reads them. The app's role
-- cannot write a bill's status, number, journal, what was withheld or what a line cleared.
--
-- Database error codes of this track are SE200 to SE299 (docs/PARALLEL.md); Step 30 used SE200
-- to SE210 and Step 24 SE211 to SE222:
--   SE223  no such supplier bill in this company (or outside the member's branches)
--   SE224  the bill is not in the state this needs
--   SE225  a posted bill is never changed or removed
--   SE226  a line is written only while its bill is a draft; a line of goods is a line of a
--          posted goods received note, from the bill's supplier, into the bill's branch
--   SE227  a bill is posted with at least one line, and figures that are its lines' and the tables'
--   SE228  more billed than was received and is not yet billed
--   SE229  sales tax on a bill needs the company and the supplier registered for it
--   SE230  no rate, or no such withholding line, in force on the bill's date
--   SE231  the company does not withhold tax (it has not switched it on)
--   SE232  the supplier's invoice number is already on a posted bill of that supplier
--   SE233  a date that has not come yet, or is no day on the calendar
--   SE234  the account cannot be charged by a bill
-- SE219 (purchase documents are written in read committed transactions) is Step 24's, used again.

